just one year ago today nevada's first  confirmed covid patient also known as  patient zero was admitted to the  hospital joe moeller was there  covering this story one year ago and  today he spoke to him  about how far we have come he brings us  a story from the v.a hospital up in  north las vegas  when ronald pimpkins came here to the va  copin 19 did not even cross his mind now  one year later  he has a message for others  i think about those days leading up to  actually going to the hospital in  february 2020 ronald pimpkins went on a  trip with family to washington  i had no taste  um the actual last night i was  in washington seattle i had shivers  and i was cold and i didn't know what  was up it wasn't until he returned home  to las vegas when things got worse  on march 2nd he went to the va hospital  after being here  less than an hour they said my oxygen  level was very low  he was put in a coma as doctors tried to  figure out what was wrong  that's the last i remember until i woke  up at the end of march  pipkins was diagnosed with coping 19. he  did not get out of the hospital until  april  thank goodness that the governor put the  restrictions in place that he did  because if he wouldn't have  so many people in the state of nevada  would have died last week pipkins  received the copa 19 vaccine my daughter  went through so much  so much pain mentally of seeing her dad  lay in a coma  i i said to myself for my family  i'll i'll do it with three vaccines  available he helps more people  get their shot i wasn't given the  opportunity  to safeguard myself from this virus  but we all have that opportunity now  and so we all come together as a nation  we can get rid of this virus and we can  get on with our lives  pimpkins also thanked the staff and  medical professionals here at the va who  he says  saved his life reporting in north las  vegas joe moeller 8 news now
 

